      "finding": "write finished text. This one works in both directions: it shapes prose *as it's generated* so the patterns never appear, and it cleans existing text when you paste some in. It knows a cold email shou",
      "explanation": "Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.",
      "remediation": "Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.",
      "code_snippet": "\nA skill that makes AI-assisted text read like a person wrote it, while writing rather than only after the fact, plus a deterministic linter that scores any text for AI-pattern density.\n\nMost tools in this space rewrite finished text. This one works in both directions: it shapes prose *as it's generated* so the patterns never appear, and it cleans existing text when you paste some in. It knows a cold email shouldn't be humanized like a formal report, it can learn *your* voice from a few paragraphs of your writing, and it ships with a stdlib-only Python linter you can run in CI.\n\nIt is not tied to any one assistant. The skill is plain Markdown in the open [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io) format, so it works in Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Codex CLI, Amp, and any other harness that reads a `SKILL.md`. The linter is a standalone script that needs nothing but Python.\n",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Rogue Agent"
      ],
